---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Validation"
  description="Tested contracts and the limits of this release."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Validation</h1><p>Compatibility is tested, not assumed.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Release checks</h2><ul>
      <li>
        Packaged exports, types and selective imports. Consumers install
        tarballs outside the workspace.
      </li>
      <li>
        React 18/19: controlled forms, native events, reset, FormData, refs,
        router links and Strict Mode cleanup.
      </li>
      <li>
        Next.js 16 / React 19: App Router, request-time SSR, hydration and the
        complete notes flow.
      </li>
      <li>
        Vue 3 / Svelte 5: properties, events and slots in executable Vite
        consumers.
      </li>
      <li>
        Chromium, Firefox and WebKit: keyboard, focus and component behavior.
        Automated accessibility checks accompany visual regression tests.
      </li>
      <li>Node 22/24 in CI; minimum tooling version 22.12.</li>
    </ul><p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/andrewsrigom/caderno-ui/actions/workflows/ci.yml"
        >Inspect CI results</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Limits</h2><ul>
      <li>
        Client boundaries preserve server-rendered slotted HTML, not Lit
        shadow-root SSR. Internal form controls need JavaScript.
      </li>
      <li>
        The public notes app is a static export, not a running Next.js server.
        Its local data never leaves the browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        Nuxt, SvelteKit, new framework adapters and 1.0 API stability are not
        part of this release.
      </li>
      <li>
        Automated accessibility checks do not establish screen-reader
        compatibility. NVDA, VoiceOver and JAWS combinations are not advertised
        as verified without a recorded manual session.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
